{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "A double-decker bus operated by Stagecoach South West overturned on the A385 between Totnes and Paignton while traveling from Torquay to Plymouth at about 11:00 BST."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "Police reported up to eight people seriously injured, and 37 people were taken to several hospitals in Devon for treatment."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "Emergency services closed the road, declared a major incident (later stood down), sent several ambulances and the air ambulance, and a witness described seeing emergency vehicles everywhere."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "Uninjured passengers were taken to Paignton bus station for support and to continue their journeys."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "The road will remain closed in both directions for several hours for investigation and recovery, said fire service area manager Gerald Taylor."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "Police said the bus driver had not been arrested and was assisting with inquiries; Stagecoach South West stated they are assisting the investigation and that safety is their priority."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "Jane Viner, chief nurse, thanked all NHS staff who came in on their day off, and MP Sarah Wollaston thanked the emergency services for their efforts."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "The Portuguese Episcopal Conference announced the suspension of public Masses from Jan. 23, citing the extreme gravity of the pandemic."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "Portugal has recorded over 609,000 COVID-19 cases and 9,920 deaths as of Jan. 22, amid a surge in deaths."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "This is the second time the bishops have suspended public worship; the first was in March 2020 and was eased at the end of May."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "The bishops suspended catechesis and other pastoral activities requiring gatherings, and called on priests to livestream Masses."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "Earlier in January, the bishops had called for the suspension or postponement of baptisms, confirmations, and marriages."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "Funerals may be celebrated according to norms from May 2020 requiring social distancing."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "A Lenten retreat for the bishops, scheduled for Feb. 22-26, was canceled."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "The Shrine of Our Lady of Fatima will broadcast three Masses and two rosaries daily during the suspension."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "subevent": "Shrine rector Fr. Carlos Cabecinhas said that while it is not the same as physical presence, it is the only way to participate now."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "Clashes broke out Sunday in Jerusalem's Mea Shearim as police attempted to shut down a yeshiva that opened illegally; hundreds surrounded officers, shouting insults and throwing debris, leading to one arrest and water cannon deployment."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "In Ashdod, police were confronted while closing an ultra-Orthodox elementary school that opened illegally; dozens tried to force entry, injuring four officers and damaging the fence, and four people were arrested."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "In Bnei Brak, clashes occurred as police tried to shut down schools linked to the Vizhnitz Hasidic dynasty, whose head rabbi initially ruled that educational institutions should open but backtracked hours later."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "Police said in response to the violence that they would continue to enforce virus restrictions in all communities."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "The lockdown, extended to January 31, has shuttered nonessential businesses and the entire education system, but some ultra-Orthodox schools have continued to operate in violation."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "Last week, a mob in Bnei Brak injured a police officer, leading to six arrests; Prime Minister Netanyahu condemned the attack, but critics accused him of avoiding a crackdown on the ultra-Orthodox to keep his coalition partners happy."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "Additional lockdown violations emerged, including a mass gathering in the Sanz Hasidic sect in Netanya, and other sects are expected to hold prayers and gatherings; Health Minister Yuli Edelstein called for jailing those who broke lockdown rules."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "Netanyahu and Edelstein appealed to Rabbi Chaim Kanievsky, who gave permission for some ultra-Orthodox schools to reopen but only if it does not spark a confrontation with police, though some schools were hesitant."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "subevent": "The Health Ministry reported a decline in daily infections, with 2,394 new cases Saturday, while noting that Haredi communities have suffered disproportionately from the coronavirus with higher infection rates."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "The New Horizons spacecraft flew by Pluto in July 2015."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "Researchers observed a variety of terrains across Pluto, including jagged spikes at high altitudes."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "New research found that the blades are made mostly of methane ice and form similarly to Earth's penitentes."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "The spikes form at high altitudes where methane freezes directly from gas to solid, and during warmer periods, parts of the methane ice sublimate back to gas."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "Jeffrey Moore explained that Pluto's climate variation causes methane ice to evaporate."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "On Earth, similar structures called penitentes are only a few meters tall and form at high altitudes near the equator."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "Slight irregularities in snow lead to longer spikes due to differential sublimation."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "The presence of penitentes on Pluto helps researchers understand surface temperature changes and map topography."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "subevent": "The new study will be published in the journal Icarus."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "A South West Aviation Let L-410, registration UR-TWO, crashed into Yirol Lake near Yirol City while on approach, killing 20 people and leaving 3 survivors."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "Initial rescue efforts by local fishermen recovered 19 bodies, and 4 survivors were taken to a hospital with serious injuries."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "On Sep 10 2018, authorities reported that 20 people had died and 3 survived, and Eastern Lake State declared three days of national mourning."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "The Aviation Herald received a passenger manifest showing the operator was South West Aviation, listing 17 adults and 3 children, including citizens of Uganda, Ethiopia, and South Sudan."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "Italian media reported that an Italian doctor working for an NGO in South Sudan was among the survivors and was taken to Juba with serious injuries."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "The aircraft, MSN 841328, had been previously operated by Universal-Avia and later owned by SlavAir, with tail number UR-TWO assigned on Apr 11 2018."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "On Nov 19 2018, Ukraine's NBAAI reported the accident, stating that 20 people were killed and 3 injured, and that they had assigned an accredited representative and read out parametric data from the flight data recorder."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "On Oct 23 2019, Ukraine's NBAAI published the final report from South Sudan's Ministry of Transport, concluding probable causes were severe weather, pilot error in setting the altimeter, and replacement of a faulty propeller without informing safety authorities."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "A report claims climate change can still be tackled if people embrace major lifestyle shifts, and it provides a list of the best ways to reduce carbon footprints based on an analysis of 7,000 studies."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "The report notes that public willingness to accept radical change has been shown by the Covid-19 crisis, and that government priorities must be reordered with protecting the planet as the first duty."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "The top recommended action is living car-free (saves 2.04 tonnes CO2e per person annually), followed by driving a battery electric car (1.95 tonnes) and taking one less long-haul flight (1.68 tonnes)."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "Switching to a vegan diet saves 0.8 tonnes but less than transport, and popular activities like recycling save only 0.01 tonnes and are worthwhile but less effective."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "Lead author Dr Diana Ivanova says a complete change of mindset is needed, that the top 10 options are available without expensive new technologies, and that rich people who fly and drive big cars consume the most, calling aviation under-taxed a moral issue."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "She ranks other actions: buying renewable power and public transport (4th and 5th), insulating home (6th, 0.895 tonnes), vegan diet (7th, 0.8 tonnes), and other top actions like heat pumps and renewable heating."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "Dr Ivanova estimates that implementing these measures would save around 9 tonnes CO2e per person per year, compared to current household emissions of 10 tonnes in the UK and 17 in the US."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "The study lists lesser-impact actions: green roofs, using less paper, buying durable items, turning down the thermostat, and recycling."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "subevent": "Some findings are questioned; polls show varying public views. Professor Tommy Wiedmann says the study is valuable but overlooks impacts like water scarcity from lithium mining. Libby Peake says people should keep recycling and that better design can reduce consumption and carbon footprints."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "Muslims accept that capital punishment is a punishment established by God in the Qur'an, and that it is acceptable when required by law despite murder being a sin."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "The Prophet Muhammad sentenced people to death for murder, which is a reason Muslims accept the death penalty."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "Shari'ah law states that the punishment for murder, adultery, and denying Islam is the death penalty."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "Some Muslims argue against capital punishment because although it is allowed in the Qur'an, they do not think it is compulsory."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "Shari'ah law allows the family of a murder victim to accept money as reparation instead of enforcing the death penalty."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "Some Muslims believe that only Allah has the right to take life, so carrying out the death penalty is 'playing God' and committing shirk."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "Alicia Soto attended the 1 October Sunrise Remembrance Ceremony for the third year to help process her trauma."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "Soto said she lost a part of herself that night and decided to live life to the fullest for those who died."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "A slideshow displayed the names and pictures of the 58 people killed and two additional women who died within the past year from injuries."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "Clark County Sheriff Joe Lombardo announced that Kimberly Gervais and Samanta Arjune will be added to the official death toll, raising it to 60."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "The announcement followed a Review-Journal article that highlighted their deaths and Metro's initial decision not to include them."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "Lombardo said he is comfortable acknowledging the two individuals lost their lives as a result of 1 October."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "The ceremony had fewer attendees due to the pandemic, and Gov. Steve Sisolak prioritized the event."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "Sisolak gave a speech with a shaky voice, saying we will never forget what happened."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "subevent": "Albert Rivera, father of victim Jordyn Rivera, thanked survivors, acknowledged Greg Zanis, and called for unity."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "President Joko Widodo requested a suspension of revisions to the Coal and Mineral Mining Law last year, but deliberations resumed under a new working committee of DPR and government members."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "The proposed revisions were widely criticized for pandering to the coal mining industry and threatening communities and the environment, and students demanded their rejection in protests across Indonesia in late September 2019."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "On 25 September 2019, the Ministry of Energy and Natural Resources submitted a list of 938 concerns, and the DPR abandoned plans to push the revisions through after public pressure and Jokowi's call for delay."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "Incoming DPR members (55% returning) resumed discussions, with a working committee agreeing on 235 of 703 proposed changes, while the draft remained unchanged from the previous year."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "The revisions ease permit processes, allow companies to extend permits without offering concessions to state-owned firms, remove the 15,000-hectare cap on concession areas, and permit multiple permits per province for the same commodity."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "The revisions drop prison terms for officials who approve problematic permits and add fines and prison terms for anyone hindering mining activities, while removing communities' right to veto mining."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "The revisions end company responsibility for site rehabilitation, proposing that abandoned pits be used for irrigation or tourism, despite 3,033 pits left unfilled from 2014–2018 causing 140 deaths, and ignore disaster risk reduction, exacerbating floods like Samarinda's 150 flood events from 2009–2014."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "The revisions privilege coal as a commodity, conflicting with climate commitments and Indonesia's goal to reduce coal reliance, as coal still constituted 60% of the energy mix in 2018."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "In December 2020, scientists published a paper describing the dinosaur Ubirajara jubatus from a fossil housed in Germany."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "Brazilian paleontologists questioned the legality of the fossil's export from Brazil and demanded its return, leading to the temporary withdrawal of the paper on December 24, 2020."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "The Baden-Württemberg ministry backed the museum's ownership claim, stating the fossil was legally acquired, which outraged the Brazilian paleontology community."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "Cretaceous Research permanently retracted the paper due to unresolved export permission concerns."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "The journal updated its policy to reject papers on fossils of uncertain or illegal provenance."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "The retraction rekindled Brazilian demands for the fossil's repatriation, and the ministry said it would reexamine the process."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "A preprint analysis showed that many paleontology papers involving fossils from developing countries lack local authors, a practice called parachute science."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "Some paleontologists argued that fossils are safer in European and U.S. museums, while Brazilian scientists countered that they have adequate infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "subevent": "Other researchers voluntarily repatriated Brazilian fossils, including a spider fossil from the University of Kansas."
    },
    {
      "id": "9",
      "subevent": "Scientists noted that the retraction leaves the species nonexistent to science, calling it a second extinction."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "NASA's Spitzer Space Telescope captured enough light from exoplanets to identify molecules in their atmospheres for the first time."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "This landmark achievement came years before astronomers anticipated and is a significant step toward detecting life on rocky exoplanets."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "Spitzer obtained spectra for two hot Jupiters, HD 209458b and HD 189733b."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "The data show the planets are drier and cloudier than predicted, with no water detected and hints of silicates in HD 209458b's atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "Three teams of astronomers used Spitzer to capture exoplanet spectra, all with similar results."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "The secondary eclipse technique was used to isolate the planets' light from their stars."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "Previous Hubble observations of HD 209458b revealed individual elements and less sodium than predicted, supporting the presence of high clouds."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "Astronomers plan to use Spitzer for further studies of transiting exoplanets and eventually to look for life molecules on rocky planets."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "President Donald Trump’s import tariffs will do more harm than good to the U.S. economy, say the vast majority of economists polled by Reuters."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "Nearly 90 percent of 71 respondents said they were concerned tariffs on steel and aluminum imports would lead to a wider trade war, including almost a third who said they were “very concerned.”"
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "Nearly 80 percent of 60 economists who answered a question on the tariffs said they would do more harm than good and the rest said it would do nothing or very little; not one respondent said they would benefit the U.S. economy."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "The Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development on Tuesday raised its global growth forecasts to the highest since 2011 but warned the world economy was vulnerable to trade tensions after the import tariffs."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "The latest poll showed the U.S. central bank will raise the federal funds rate by 25 basis points at the March 20-21 meeting and repeat that move three more times, taking the base rate to 2.25-2.50 percent by end-2018."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "The Fed’s preferred gauge of inflation, the core PCE price index, was forecast to reach the central bank’s 2 percent target in the third quarter and rise slightly above that next year."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "Economic growth forecasts were raised, with full-year median forecasts of 2.8 percent for 2018 and 2.4 percent for 2019."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "While most economists said fiscal stimulus from tax cuts and additional spending would benefit the economy this year they were mostly split on if it had brought the next downturn closer."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "subevent": "The median probability of a recession in the coming year was 13 percent, a slight increase from 10 percent in a November poll."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
